    "reasoning": "A1's nonlinear delta is exactly 0.000 (mathematically guaranteed: a tree probe is invariant to any monotonic transform of a feature it already has -- raw_total_reconstructed is a monotonic transform of size_contribution, already in F0). This makes A1's nonlinear result a construction-guaranteed control, not empirical evidence, and confirms section 1's invertibility finding rather than adding new information. A1's linear gain (+0.036) is a known artifact of linear models being sensitive to nonlinear reshapings of an existing input, not missing information. A8 (decomposed into 3 separate features) adds far more than A1 in both probes -- nonlinear +0.050 vs A1's +0.000, linear +0.086 beyond A1's own gain. The saturation transform (confirmed invertible, section 1) is not the information-loss source; collapsing three distinguishable primitives into one L1-summed scalar is."
